# ==========================================================================
# CVE-2026-42504 — Go stdlib (kubectl v1.35.5 / cosign earlier 3.x)
# ==========================================================================
#
# Tracking: https://groups.google.com/g/golang-dev (Go security mailing
# list — patched in Go 1.25.11 / 1.26.4). Surfaced 2026-06-09 in
# pipeline #9795 vuln-scan-tools-image (this MR's bump-cosign-3.1.1 also
# clears the cosign half if the rebuild uses Go 1.25.11+; kubectl half
# remains until v1.35.6 ships from upstream — no date announced).
#
# THREAT MODEL
# ------------
# CVE-2026-42504 is in encoding/asn1 — denial-of-service on attacker-
# controlled ASN.1 input. The keystone-tools image is consumed ONLY by
# the in-cluster `keystone-soak` CronJob, which:
#   - Runs `kubectl get/apply` against trusted in-cluster API (no
#     external ASN.1 parsing surface)
#   - Runs `cosign verify` against trusted Harbor-signed images
#     (signature DER is from a controlled set of issuers — not
#     attacker-controlled input)
# A DoS on these CronJob invocations would surface as a single missed
# soak window, which the next 15-min cron run recovers from. Not a
# security risk for this deployment.
#
# REMOVAL TRIGGER
# ---------------
# When kubectl v1.35.6 ships (Go 1.25.11+) AND cosign v3.x next minor
# rebuilds on Go 1.25.11+ AND trivy stops flagging this CVE against the
# rebuilt image, remove this block entirely. ETA: weeks (Kubernetes
# 1.35.6 cherry-pick deadline is the gating event).
CVE-2026-42504
